.TH NOXFORGE-DOCTOR 1 "August 2026" "NoxForge 9.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
noxforge-doctor \- inspect a NoxForge installation without changing it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B noxforge-doctor
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR path ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B noxforge-doctor
reports the installed package version, component provenance and versions,
safely readable active theme names, icon inheritance, actual per-output scales,
and the effective login surface when it can be detected.
It does not write files, apply a theme, clear caches, restart services, switch
display managers, or request privileges.
.PP
JSON schema 2 contains stable
.B edition
and
.B loginSurface
objects. The latter reports the manager, service state, integration type,
asset availability, selection, and status. An installed SDDM theme is not
reported as active when Plasma Login Manager is active. Unselected optional
login assets do not make the installation incomplete.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine-readable JSON.
.TP
.BI \-\-root " path"
Inspect an absolute staged or system root instead of the running system.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 for a complete, version-consistent installation, 1 for an absent,
partial, or mixed-version installation, and 2 for invalid command arguments.
.SH PRIVACY
The report omits usernames, hostnames, personal paths, and display contents.
It never treats QT_SCALE_FACTOR as per-output evidence.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/noxforge/VERSION
Expected installed NoxForge version.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rpm (8),
.BR dnf (8)
